ntor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MISAKI MASAFUMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIRAISHI MITSURU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKADA SHIGEYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUKUMOTO, SHOJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MISAKI, MASAFUMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIRAISHI, MITSURU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKADA, SHIGEYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Pernasal preparations characterized by containing a compound of general formula (I) having an Na/H exchange inhibiting activity or a salt thereof exhibit excellent bioabsorbability and an Na/H exchange inhibiting activity superior to those of peroral preparations, thus being useful as preventive and/or therapeutic agents for ischemic heart diseases such as myocardial infarct and arrhythmia: wherein A is an optionally substituted five- or six-membered aromatic heterocycle; B is an optionally substituted five- or six-membered aromatic homo- or hetero-cycle; R&lt;1&gt; is hydrogen, hydroxyl, or lower alkyl; and n is 0 or 1.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention concerne des préparations à administrer par voie nasale caractérisées en ce qu'elles renferment un composé de la formule (I) présentant une activité inhibitrice des échanges Na/H ou un sel de ce composé. Ces préparations, qui présentent une excellente biostabilité et une activité inhibitrice des échanges Na/H supérieure à celle de préparations per os, sont donc utiles en tant qu'agents préventifs et/ou thérapeutiques des cardiopathies ischémiques telles que l'infarctus du myocarde et l'arythmie cardiaque. Dans la formule (I), A représente un hétérocycle aromatique éventuellement substitué à cinq ou six éléments; B représente un homo- ou hétérocycle éventuellement substitué à cinq ou six éléments; R1 est hydrogène, hydroxyle, ou alkyle inférieur : et n vaut 0 ou 1.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>